  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In April 2023, the Confederation of Employers of Uzbekistan (CEU) adopted its first strategic plan since its establishment  in 2018. The strategic plan endeavours to promote a more structured and systematic operation of CEU, and thereby enhancing the quality of CEU`s outputs and fortifying its position as a robust employers&#x2019; organization. The strategic plan is based on a thorough self-assessment and a SWOT analysis conducted during a strategic planning workshop (May 2022),  as well as on a membership needs assessment   conducted in 2022.

In May 2023, CEU developed a membership acquisition action plan. This plan contains a targeted list of companies ranked in accordance with their importance for potential membership. The membership acquisition action plan aligns with a key objective of CEU`s strategic plan, namely increasing the number of CEU members and improving its membership structure. 

A current weakness of CEU`s membership structure is its heavy reliance on association membership rather than direct company membership. To rectify this imbalance, the action plan strives to establish a more diverse and balanced membership structure for CEU. This shift aims to enhance CEU&#x2019;s organizational resilience, foster a more diverse funding structure and cultivate heightened engagement of private companies in CEU&#x2019;s governance and activities.

In June 2023, CEU achieved another milestone by launching its first website since its establishment. This website will significantly improve the visibility of CEU and its activities. It also represents an important tool for CEU to make its policy positions and proposals better known, which would support its policy endeavours and membership expansion. The ILO supported CEU by offering technical guidance in organizing its strategic planning workshop. During the workshop, CEU secretariat staff and board   members received training on strategic planning. Additionally, the ILO offered technical advice for the formulation of the first draft CEU&#x2019;s strategic plan. Through this support, CEU acquired the necessary knowledge and skills set enabling it to finalize and adopt its strategic plan.
In partnership with ITC-ILO, the ILO provided training for three representatives of the CEU secretariat in July 2022, focusing on membership development and the organization of member needs assessments . This capacity building intervention enabled CEU to conduct a member needs assessment and develop a priority list for membership acquisition, both of which became integral parts of CEU`s membership acquisition action plan.

Furthermore, the ILO provided technical expertise to CEU on developing a website tailored to the needs of an employers` organization. As a result, CEU was equipped to develop a concept of its new website that met all its specific needs. On this basis, a web developer provided by the ILO constructed the new CEU website. The web developer critically provided training to the CEU secretariat staff on how to use, maintain and update the new website.</narrative>
   </description>
